Let parse_Rd() return on two kinds of Rd input it looped on forever, so
the rd target stops timing out and running out of memory:

- input that ends inside an [option], a \Sexpr{} body or the second
  argument of \eqn, \deqn or \figure.  In src/library/tools/src/gramRd.y,
  Arg recovers from the end of the input after an error through
  '{' ArgItems error END_OF_INPUT; Option, RLikeArg2 and VerbatimArg2 had
  no such alternative.  Error recovery there discarded END_OF_INPUT and
  read on, and con_getc() returns a newline at every other read past the
  end, so the parse never finished.  Give the three rules the same
  alternative.
- a backslash before anything but a letter, '{', '}', '%' or '\' inside
  an [option], as in \link[=foo\_bar]{x}.  mkText() fell through from its
  '\\' case to case ']', which stops the token in an option and left the
  backslash unread, so the lexer returned empty TEXT tokens forever.  Add
  the missing break.

gramRd.c is regenerated with bison 3.8.2.

Found by the rd target: the first by its first local runs, which is why rd
was deferred; the second by a run with the first fixed.

Upstream status: r-devel/r-svn PR #516, R Bugzilla 19346 (both
2026-11-19).
Delete this patch once the fix lands in R trunk (ossfuzz.sh will report
it as already-applied in the meantime, which is harmless).

